# Copy this file to deploy/.secrets.env on the server and fill it in:
#
#     cp deploy/.secrets.example.env deploy/.secrets.env
#     nano deploy/.secrets.env
#     sudo python3 deploy/dsr_deploy.py
#
# Only the mail settings belong here. The database passwords and the
# encryption key are generated by the deploy script on its first run and
# kept in /opt/dsr/server/.env from then on -- do not put them here and do
# not change them there, because the encryption key is the only copy and
# every saved setting is encrypted with it.
#
# deploy/.secrets.env is gitignored. This example file is not. Never put a
# real client secret in this one.


# --- Microsoft Graph, for sending mail ---------------------------------------
#
# The portal sends verification links to data subjects and notifications to
# your team. It does that through Microsoft Graph, as an application: no
# mailbox password, no SMTP.
#
# Without these the deployment still runs and the portal still works -- you
# can sign in, open cases, and browse. What does not work is outbound mail,
# so a data subject cannot complete the email-verification step of the
# public form. Fill these in and run the script again to switch mail on.
#
# Where each value comes from, in the Azure portal under
# Microsoft Entra ID > App registrations > your app:
#
#   GRAPH_TENANT_ID    Overview > Directory (tenant) ID
#   GRAPH_CLIENT_ID    Overview > Application (client) ID
#   GRAPH_CLIENT_SECRET  Certificates & secrets > New client secret > Value
#                        (copy it immediately -- Azure shows it once)
#
# The app registration needs the APPLICATION permission Mail.Send, granted
# with admin consent. Delegated Mail.Send will not work: there is no signed-in
# user. Your tenant may also restrict which mailboxes an app may send as,
# through an application access policy -- if mail fails with ErrorAccessDenied
# once the values are right, that policy is where to look.

PRIVACY_MAILBOX=privacy@yourcompany.com
GRAPH_TENANT_ID=
GRAPH_CLIENT_ID=
GRAPH_CLIENT_SECRET=


# --- Optional ----------------------------------------------------------------

# graph   send mail through the values above (the default)
# console do not send at all -- what the script falls back to when the four
#         values above are empty, so the portal still deploys and runs
# EMAIL_PROVIDER=graph

# Set this to true once TLS is installed, so the admin session cookie is only
# ever sent over HTTPS. Leave it alone while the portal is on plain HTTP: a
# Secure cookie over HTTP is not sent at all, and nobody can sign in.
# Install TLS with deploy/enable-tls.sh, or deploy/enable-tls-ip.sh for a host
# with no domain name.
# COOKIE_SECURE=true
